ThumbyScummby
=============

A SCUMM v4/v5 interpreter port targeting the Thumby Color handheld
(RP2350, 128x128 RGB565 LCD, 520 KB SRAM).

Licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later. See LICENSE for full terms.

Derived From
------------

The interpreter logic in this project is a port of ScummVM
(https://www.scummvm.org/), the Graphic Adventure Engine, also
licensed GPL-3.0-or-later. ScummVM's `engines/scumm/` source tree is
included under `scummvm-upstream/` as the reference specification
this port mirrors. Where individual files in `engine/src/` and
`engine/include/` reproduce algorithms, constants, opcode dispatch
tables, resource layouts, or other behavioural details from
ScummVM, inline comments cite the upstream `file:line` they were
ported from.

Credit for the interpreter design, the SCUMM bytecode disassembly
and behavioural reverse-engineering, and the resource format work
goes to the ScummVM developers and contributors. See
`scummvm-upstream/COPYRIGHT` for their full author list.

The original SCUMM engine and the games it interprets are the
intellectual property of LucasArts / Lucasfilm Games / their
successors. This port is a software interpreter only and ships no
game data — users must supply their own legitimately-acquired data
files.

Files Outside This Port
-----------------------

- `scummvm-upstream/` — unmodified upstream snapshot, kept under its
  own license terms (see `scummvm-upstream/COPYING` and
  `scummvm-upstream/COPYRIGHT`).
- `data/` — game data files supplied by the user; not part of this
  source distribution.
